      "type": "mcq",
      "question": "Mawia says, “If you reverse the digits of my age, the number that you obtain will be Zova’s age. Zova is older than I am and the difference of my age and that of Zova’s will be one-eleventh of the sum of our ages.” The age of Mawia is",
      "options": [
        "23 years",
        "34 years",
        "45 years",
        "None of these"
      ],
      "answerIndex": 2,
      "answerSource": "derived",
      "answerKeyRef": null,
      "explanation": "Let Mawia be 10a+b and Zova 10b+a. The difference 9(b−a) equals one-eleventh of their sum, a+b. Thus 8b=10a, or 4b=5a; digit constraints give a=4,b=5, so Mawia is 45, option (c). Independently checked solution, unofficial. No matching examiner answer key is asserted.",
